.venv/
__pycache__/
.cache/
.DS_Store
data.json
report.html
# Generated at runtime and full of real names and email addresses. Treat every file in
# this group as personal data: after a collect run it can hold the identity of everyone
# in your org. Check `git status` before committing.
#
# Worth knowing, because it is the reason this block is so emphatic: people.yaml was
# TRACKED in an earlier, internal history of this tool, and the app rewrote it at
# runtime — so a test fixture got committed over it, and was then imported back into the
# override table as if it were curated data. Nothing reads or writes that file now.
identity_suggestions.yaml
other-people.md
people.yaml
config.local.yaml
config-editor.html
identity-editor.html
history/people/
history/config/
_site/
.repos/
.runtime/
exports/
.env
.claude/
.playwright-mcp/
# SQLite store lives on the docker bind-mount (persists across restarts).
#
# `**/` and not `history/`, which would anchor these to the repo root. store.connect()
# resolves DATA_DIR from the CURRENT working directory, so running anything from backend/
# creates backend/history/report.db — a path an anchored pattern does not match, and one
# that got committed once before this comment existed. The store may hold the identity of
# everyone in the org, so where it happens to sit must not decide whether git tracks it.
# EVERY database under a history/ directory, whatever it is called. This started as a list
# of exact names (report.db, prod-copy.db), then grew a `*-copy.db` wildcard when it became
# clear pull-db.sh accepts any destination — and that was still a guess about the name.
# Pulling a snapshot to `prod-copy.new.db` for a moment, to avoid clobbering the previous
# one, produced a 255 MB file holding 138 people's identities that git offered to track.
# The rule is not "these names are private", it is "a database here is private", so match
# on the extension and its SQLite sidecars instead of on anybody's naming discipline.
**/history/*.db
**/history/*.db-shm
**/history/*.db-wal

# Collected aggregates. These were TRACKED internally as a "text backup of the DB" and
# that was a mistake for a public repo: snapshots.jsonl carries per-company commit / LOC
# / headcount figures and traffic.jsonl carries private repo names. Both are collected
# output about your org, not source — back them up outside git.
history/*.jsonl

# oauth2-proxy break-glass basic-auth (secret) — keep the .example only
deploy/oauth/htpasswd

# React frontend (frontend/) — Vite build output is baked by the Docker frontend
# stage, not committed. Keep assets/app/.gitkeep so the dir exists pre-build.
frontend/node_modules/
assets/app/*
!assets/app/.gitkeep

# Screenshot-diff harness (frontend/visual/) — screenshots are generated
# artifacts, not committed. Keep the scripts + routes manifest + README.
frontend/visual/baseline/
frontend/visual/candidate/
frontend/visual/diff/

# per-installation deploy target (host/key/dir) — never in git
scripts/deploy.env

# Design mockups served against the real stylesheets (scripts serve the repo root).
# Throwaway by nature and often carry pulled data — not source.
mockups/
